# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

Always enforce permissions on the **backend** with guards from
`apps/backend/src/middleware/authorize.ts`. UI-only checks are not sufficient.

## Guards

| Guard | Who passes | Use for |
| ----- | ---------- | ------- |
| `shouldBeGuest()` | guest, user, admin | Authenticated read access |
| `shouldBeUser()` | user, admin | Registered-user mutations |
| `shouldBeAdmin()` | admin only | Full admin mutations |

Routes must `.use(setup)` before role guards so `currentUser` is available.

## Permission matrix

| Action | guest | user | admin |
| ------ | ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Read novels, keywords, replacements, categories, natures, chapters | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Create/edit/delete keyword | No | Own only | Yes |
| Create/edit/delete replacement | No | No | Yes |
| Add novel | No | name + slugs only | Yes (full) |
| Edit novel | No | add slug only (`slugs` field) | Yes (full) |
| Delete novel | No | No | Yes |
| Edit own profile (`PUT /auth/me`) | Yes (onboarding) | Yes | Yes |
| Manage categories, natures, chapters, configs | No | No | Yes |
| Upload files | No | Yes | Yes |

## Ownership

For user-owned resources (keywords), use `assertOwnsResource(createdById, authedUser)`
after `shouldBeUser()` on update/delete.

## Uniqueness

- Keywords: unique `(name, novelId)` per novel
- Replacements: unique `(from, novelId)` per novel

## When adding new routes

1. Pick the lowest guard that matches the matrix above.
2. Apply `assertOwnsResource` when users may only touch their own rows.
3. Restrict request body fields in handlers when users have partial edit rights
   (e.g. user novel create: name + slugs only).
4. If the matrix does not cover a new action, **ask the user** before implementing.

## Extension UI

Mirror backend rules in the UI (hide/disable actions), but never rely on UI alone.
